00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.542
If you've been
watching the keynotes,

00:00:10.542 --> 00:00:12.410
SAP's got a lot of
attention from us.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.250
Without going into all
the detail, in fact

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.413
I am actually doing a
speech tomorrow afternoon

00:00:19.413 --> 00:00:21.330
talking about where we
are technology-wise and

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.107
platform-wise with SAP.

00:00:23.107 --> 00:00:23.940
So come to that one.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.715
Bring your friends.

00:00:25.715 --> 00:00:27.840
So without going into all
that detail, all I'll say

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.070
is we've come a long
way in 12 months.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.350
So nine months ago
at Next San Francisco

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.780
last year, we launched
the 4-terabyte servers

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.380
with the promise that we'd have
the 12 terabytes this year,

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.555
and then the 18 terabytes.

00:00:41.555 --> 00:00:42.930
Obviously, we
announced yesterday

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.138
we've made the 12 terabytes
available to early access

00:00:45.138 --> 00:00:46.590
customers.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:50.390
That's just a huge [INAUDIBLE]
the only 12-terabyte VMs

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.700
in market, the
largest VMs in market.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.550
We really are setting the pace
for the industry at this point.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.440
And then from a
customer perspective,

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.090
I have to tell you,
my objective here

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.900
was not just to go out
and randomly take anyone.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.390
My objective was, look,
I've been in this market

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:07.110
a long time.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.050
What happens generally for SAP
customers is they come to you

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:13.230
and say, well, I know you have
a customer that's like me,

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.970
but I'm bigger than them.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.528
And so are you really--
can you handle me?

00:01:18.528 --> 00:01:20.070
And so that was one
of our challenges

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:22.110
as we came in the
market, was how

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:25.703
do you convince this market
that we're serious about SAP

00:01:25.703 --> 00:01:27.870
and that we can handle
everybody without this taking

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:29.920
five years for us to build.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.550
And so objective number
one for me was, let's

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.930
not just go find anyone.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:37.650
Let's take the largest customers
that we can find, and let's

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.900
convince them that, A, Google
Cloud is serious, and B,

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.210
we can run their
SAP environments.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.673
And we did that.

00:01:43.673 --> 00:01:45.090
As you're about
to see here, we've

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:46.890
rolled out a bunch
of names already,

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:49.080
more to come over time.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:52.320
But we got some of
the largest customers

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.793
on the planet, two of which
are represented here today.

00:01:54.793 --> 00:01:56.460
And that would be the
second part, which

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.230
is the extended part
of this strategy,

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.630
frankly, is that I
thoroughly believe

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:03.600
that SAP customers
don't actually

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.660
buy from salespeople, that SAP
customers are a giant club,

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.490
and they buy from each other.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:09.740
One of them does something.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.460
And if it's successful,
they tell all their friends,

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.420
and all their friends
choose to do it too.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.540
And so objective number
one was find the largest

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:16.860
customers on the
planet and convince

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.068
them to come to Google Cloud.

00:02:18.068 --> 00:02:21.040
Objective number two was
let them tell their stories.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.590
And so that's
today's subject, is

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.870
let's bring two
customers up on stage

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.720
to tell their story
of what they're

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.200
doing with SAP and Google Cloud
so you can learn from them

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:36.205
and hear it from the customer's
mouth instead from our mouths.

00:02:36.205 --> 00:02:37.580
So with that, I'd
like to welcome

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.268
on stage Meena Kishanchandani--

00:02:40.268 --> 00:02:41.310
I got it right this time?

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.020
I got it right both
times, apparently--

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:47.760
Meena, who is with McKesson
Technology, and Timo Salzsieder

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.580
from Metronom or Metro Group.

